.TH LOADMOD 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
loadmod \- Load a module into a region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loadmod
.I name
.RI [ region ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Load the game module
.I name
into a region, where its commands and event handlers start running. Modules
are named by stem only: a name containing a slash is refused.
.PP
The region is a bare world number (0\-65535) or the keyword \fBcosmos\fP,
under exactly the same rules as every other region selector. Without one the
command acts on your \fBdefault target region\fP (see \fBtarget\fP(10)), or
on the region you are standing in if you have set none. Regions at other
widths (districts, super\-planet regions \-\- see \fBgrant\fP(10)) are
reached through your default; see \fBtarget\fP(10) for the width\-and\-point
form.
.PP
Unlike \fBwall\fP and \fBban\fP, which are scoped to a subtree, module
loading attaches to one specific region row, so it needs exact ownership of
the named region, not merely rule over an ancestor. The region must exist.
A failed load leaves the region exactly as it was, so a typo cannot persist
and haunt every boot; a module that is already loaded says so. Loaded
modules persist in the region's row and are restored on every boot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unloadmod,modlist,release,target,planet (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
